Don't inherit the workspace's -Werror into third-party sdist builds.

pycross_wheel_build forwards the resolved C/C++ toolchain flags into
the wheel build's sysconfig (CC/CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS...), which includes
whatever copts the workspace compiles its own code with. A workspace
-Werror policy routinely breaks foreign build systems it was never
meant to govern. Concretely, with a clang toolchain:

    clang: error: argument unused during compilation: '-L../lib'
    [-Werror,-Wunused-command-line-argument]

where the harmless `-L../lib` comes from python-build-standalone's
sysconfig contribution to extension compile lines — failing every
C-extension sdist build (psutil, zope-interface, tree-sitter*, ...).

Strip `-Werror` and `-Werror=<warning>` from the CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS
handed to wheel builds; all other flags (defines, sysroot, -std,
optimization level) pass through unchanged. Third-party sdists are
not the workspace's code and shouldn't be held to its warning policy.

Applied via `single_version_override(patches=...)` on rules_pycross in
//MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to jvolkman/rules_pycross.

--- a/pycross/private/wheel_build.bzl	2026-07-24 12:57:33
+++ b/pycross/private/wheel_build.bzl	2026-07-24 12:57:33
@@ -33,6 +33,19 @@
 def _join_flags_list(workspace_name, flags):
     return " ".join([absolutize_path_in_str(workspace_name, "$$EXT_BUILD_ROOT$$/", flag) for flag in flags])
 
+def _drop_werror(flag_list):
+    """Third-party sdist builds shouldn't inherit the workspace's -Werror.
+
+    The C/C++ toolchain flags forwarded into wheel builds include whatever
+    copts the workspace compiles its own code with. Warning-as-error
+    policies routinely break foreign build systems — e.g. clang's
+    -Wunused-command-line-argument fires on the harmless `-L../lib` that
+    python-build-standalone's sysconfig contributes to extension compile
+    lines, turning every C-extension sdist build into a hard failure.
+    Keep all other flags (defines, sysroot, -std, optimization) intact.
+    """
+    return [f for f in flag_list if f != "-Werror" and not f.startswith("-Werror=")]
+
 def _get_sysconfig_data(workspace_name, tools, flags):
     cc = _absolute_tool_value(workspace_name, tools.cc)
     cxx = _absolute_tool_value(workspace_name, tools.cxx)
@@ -47,8 +60,8 @@
     vars = {
         "CC": cc,
         "CXX": cxx,
-        "CFLAGS": _join_flags_list(workspace_name, flags.cc),
-        "CXXFLAGS": _join_flags_list(workspace_name, flags.cxx),
+        "CFLAGS": _join_flags_list(workspace_name, _drop_werror(flags.cc)),
+        "CXXFLAGS": _join_flags_list(workspace_name, _drop_werror(flags.cxx)),
         "CCSHARED": "-fPIC" if flags.needs_pic_for_dynamic_libraries else "",
         "LDSHAREDFLAGS": _join_flags_list(workspace_name, flags.cxx_linker_shared),
         "AR": ar,
